{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow, so the translator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"targets SwiftUI’s "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state graph"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" — computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not imperative functions. Each row below is a rule the codegen applies; the helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"},{"type":"text","text":", …) fills the gaps where a patch has no direct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent."}]},{"level":2,"text":"The four rules","type":"heading","anchor":"The-four-rules"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Origami","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pure value patch (Add, Transition\/interpolate, logic)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"computed property \/ expression"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interaction (Tap, Down\/press, Double Tap, Long Press)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"gesture + ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"@GestureState","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.drag"},{"type":"text","text":" — Drag"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drag(enable:momentum:bounds:position:translation:velocity:reset:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (helper)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State\/memory (Switch, Sample and Hold)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" + update logic","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Animation (Classic Animation, Pop\/Spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(.spring)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Origami layer tree becomes the SwiftUI "},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" body. Origami "},{"code":"Transition","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpolation (not SwiftUI’s "},{"code":".transition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier — that’s a different concept)."}]},{"level":3,"text":"Pure value patch → computed property","type":"heading","anchor":"Pure-value-patch-%E2%86%92-computed-property"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Add"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transition\/interpolate"},{"text":", and other pure-function patches carry no state.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"They fan an input through math and emit an output. In SwiftUI that’s a computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property (or an inline expression) — no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":", no side effect.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Interaction → gesture + `@State`","type":"heading","anchor":"Interaction-%E2%86%92-gesture-+-State"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s Interaction patch exposes discrete output ports: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"down"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"position"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDoubleTap"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onLongPress"},{"type":"text","text":". Each maps to a SwiftUI gesture recognizer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose output lands in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" or fires a callback. The "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction"},{"type":"text","text":" helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attaches only the recognizer for each output the caller requests, which keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gesture arbitration clean."}]},{"level":3,"text":"State\/memory → `@State` + update logic","type":"heading","anchor":"Statememory-%E2%86%92-State-+-update-logic"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Sample and Hold","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" remember a value across evaluations. That’s what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is for. Codegen emits the state variable plus the update path (a gesture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"callback, a "},{"code":".onChange","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or an assignment inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" block).","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Animation → `withAnimation` \/ `.animation`","type":"heading","anchor":"Animation-%E2%86%92-withAnimation--animation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Classic Animation"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pop Animation"},{"text":", and other animation patches drive a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"toward a target over time. In SwiftUI, that’s a state change wrapped in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"text":" or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animation(_:value:)"},{"text":" modifier on the animated property.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Continuous-time springs that don’t have a stock SwiftUI equivalent get flagged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by the parser — Swami won’t fake them.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Flag, don’t fake","type":"heading","anchor":"Flag-dont-fake"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some Origami semantics don’t have a SwiftUI equivalent. When the parser hits one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it emits a marker in the IR and codegen surfaces the gap rather than papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. The current list: continuous-time springs, custom JavaScript patches,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absolute-position layout."}]}]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"]]},"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Drag":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/drag","abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drag"}]},{"text":" patch (","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Drag","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drag"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}]},{"text":" patch.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","title":"Interaction"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"title":"Swami","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Beats":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/beats","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four-beat discipline that keeps the translator honest: one pattern per branch,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compile-clean before opening a PR, visual gate against Origami’s own render, ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only on Reviewer approval plus a human spot-check."}],"title":"Beats","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"}}}